  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two arrays AAA and BBB, of lengths NNN and MMM respectively (M≤NM \\leq NM≤N).\n\nAll the elements of AAA are distinct, and all the elements of BBB are distinct — that is, Ai≠AjA_i \\neq A_jAi​=Aj​ for i≠ji \\neq ji=j, and Bi≠BjB_i \\neq B_jBi​=Bj​ for i≠ji \\neq ji=j.\n\nIn one operation, you can do the following:\n\n\nChoose a subarray†^\\dagger† of AAA with length MMM, and replace it with a cyclic rotation‡^\\ddagger‡ of the array BBB.\nFor instance, if A=[3,2,5,4,6]A = [3, 2, 5, 4, 6]A=[3,2,5,4,6] and B=[2,1,3]B = [2, 1, 3]B=[2,1,3], you can choose to replace the subarray [2,5,4][2, 5, 4][2,5,4] of AAA with the array [3,2,1][3, 2, 1][3,2,1] which is a cyclic shift of BBB, to obtain [3,3,2,1,6][3, 3, 2, 1, 6][3,3,2,1,6].\n\nYour task is to find the **lexicographically minimum** possible array AAA that can be obtained by performing this operation several (possibly, zero) times.\n\nAn array PPP of length NNN is lexicographically smaller than another array QQQ of the same length if and only if there exists an index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N) such that:\n\n\nPi&lt;QiP_i \\lt Q_iPi​&lt;Qi​; and\nPj=QjP_j = Q_jPj​=Qj​ for all 1≤j&lt;i1 \\leq j \\lt i1≤j&lt;i\n†^\\dagger† A subarray of an array is obtained by deleting some (possibly zero) elements from its prefix and some (possibly zero) elements from its suffix.\n\nFor example, if A=[1,3,4,2]A = [1, 3, 4, 2]A=[1,3,4,2] then [1],[3,4,2],[1], [3, 4, 2],[1],[3,4,2], and [1,3][1, 3][1,3] are some of its subarrays; whereas [1,4][1, 4][1,4] is not a subarray of AAA.\n\n‡^\\ddagger‡ A cyclic rotation of an array is obtained by repeatedly moving its first element to its end, zero or more times.\n\nFor example, the cyclic rotations of [1,3,4,2][1, 3, 4, 2][1,3,4,2] are [1,3,4,2],[3,4,2,1],[4,2,1,3],[2,1,3,4][1, 3, 4, 2], [3, 4, 2, 1], [4, 2, 1, 3], [2, 1, 3, 4][1,3,4,2],[3,4,2,1],[4,2,1,3],[2,1,3,4].\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of three lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM — the lengths of the arrays AAA and BBB, respectively.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the elements of\narray AAA.\nThe third line contains MMM space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BMB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_MB1​,B2​,…,BM​ — the elements of array BBB.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line NNN space-separated integers, denoting the lexicographically minimum array AAA that can be obtained by performing the given operation several times.",
    "constraints": [
