        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Perform these two operations:\n\nReplace subarray [4][4][4] of AAA with [2][2][2], to obtain [2,1,6][2, 1, 6][2,1,6].\nReplace subarray [6][6][6] of AAA with [2][2][2], to obtain [2,1,2][2, 1, 2][2,1,2].\n\nThis is the lexicographically smallest array that can be obtained.\nTest case 222: It's optimal to not perform any moves.\nTest case 333: Perform one operation:\n\nReplace subarray [3,7,1][3, 7, 1][3,7,1] of AAA with [3,6,4][3, 6, 4][3,6,4] (which is a cyclic rotation of BBB) to obtain [2,3,6,4][2, 3, 6, 4][2,3,6,4].\n\nThis is optimal."
